KNOWNBUG buechi
cycle_delay_star5.sv
--buechi --bound 20
^\[main\.p0\] always \(main\.c == 1 \|-> strong\(main\.c == 1 ##\[\*\] main\.c == 1\)\): PROVED up to bound 20$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
ltl_sva_to_stringt::rec (src/temporal-logic/ltl_sva_to_string.cpp)
emits "w ##[*] x" as "w : 1[*] ; x", which Spot parses as
"{w : 1[*]} ; x", i.e., x is required to start at least one cycle after
w.  The zero-delay case of ##[0:$] is lost.  EBMC reports REFUTED with
--buechi, whereas the word-level BMC encoding gives the correct result.
